{"id":"aunque","lemma":"aunque","pos":"conj","rank":295,"glosses":["though, although, even though, albeit","even if, irrespective of (followed by subjunctive verb form)"],"ipa":"/ˈaunke/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/LL-Q1321_%28spa%29-AdrianAbdulBaha-aunque.wav","examples":[{"text":"Aunque parezca extraño, falló.","en":"Strangely enough, he failed.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/735589"},{"text":"Aunque fracases, no abandones.","en":"Even if you mess up, don't give up.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/721827"},{"text":"Voy aunque llueva a cántaros.","en":"I'll go even if it rains heavily.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/767812"},{"text":"Aunque estaba cansada, siguió trabajando.","en":"Though she was tired, she kept on working.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/691391"},{"text":"Siguió trabajando aunque estaba cansada.","en":"She kept working even though she was tired.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/937557"}]}